This repository contains an implementation of an automated optimization
modeling platform and its documentation.

OptiMind's public hints and adapted inference prompts are from Microsoft
OptiGuide/optimind, commit 419cf7b9eee20b6af036abf15152fa775b20c951.
Copyright (c) 2025 Microsoft, MIT license. The original hint CSV, license,
source paths and hashes are retained in methods/optimind/source/.
BIND's workflow is adapted from SprocketLab/Text2Opt-Bench, commit
1dac06be656c41d827ef20987cf8af0b48d382a2, Copyright (c) 2026 SprocketLab,
MIT license, retained in methods/bind/LICENSE.txt.
The SAC-Opt integration is an independent implementation with newly written
prompts based on the published algorithm and reference commit
ec0ddb544ae6b70714181740ebbba16027df50e4 of Forrest-Stone/SAC-Opt.
No source code or prompt text from that unlicensed repository is bundled.

OptiTree's fixed public modeling-thought library and tree mapping are bundled
under their original MIT license in src/llm4om/methods/optitree/source/.
Copyright (c) 2025 MIRA Lab.
Upstream: https://github.com/MIRALab-USTC/OptiTree
Fixed commit: 2e70ecfd0a3c8e9c0c16d36d7d498a7344cfdec9
The original license is retained in optitree/source/LICENSE.txt; manifest.json
records original paths and byte hashes. The OptiTree prompt text in
src/llm4om/methods/optitree/prompts.py is extracted verbatim from the same
commit.
OptiMUS prompt text in src/llm4om/methods/optimus/prompts.py is extracted
verbatim from https://github.com/teshnizi/OptiMUS (commit e182e9e), MIT
license; the original license is retained in optimus/LICENSE.txt.

The Chain-of-Experts (https://github.com/xzymustbexzy/Chain-of-Experts,
commit afb89bf) and OR-LLM-Agent (https://github.com/bwz96sco/or_llm_agent,
commit 5dccdaa) adapters reproduce upstream prompt text. The AutoFormulation
adapter includes upstream source files from
https://github.com/jumpynitro/AutoFormulator (commit 5214801) in
src/llm4om/methods/autoformulation/upstream/, and ports further upstream
functions in autoformulation/search.py and autoformulation/codegen.py. The
LLMOPT prompt text in src/llm4om/methods/llmopt/prompts.py is copied verbatim
from https://github.com/antgroup/LLMOPT (commit 1492dd3), and the ORThought
prompt text in src/llm4om/methods/orthought/prompts.py from
https://github.com/BeinuoYang/ORThought (commit 5293e24). These repositories state no
license at the fixed commits; their text is included for research
reproduction only and must not be redistributed without the authors'
permission.

The TriVAL graph, nodes and prompts in src/llm4om/methods/trival/ are
ported from https://github.com/SCUT-EIPI/TriVAL (commit 380a529),
MIT license, Copyright (c) 2026 Ziyang Fang. Adaptations are listed in
src/llm4om/methods/trival/README.md.

Public benchmark question projections are bundled in
src/llm4om/server/examples_data/ from the user's prepared OPT-Agent data.
Source: https://github.com/Fangziyang0910/OPT-Agent
Fixed commit: ad1c15bed95af0efc7de7d28c38baf2ad2f12351
catalog.json records the source paths, byte hashes and question counts.
Only existing managers' get_input() outputs and sample IDs are retained;
answers, reference solutions and solver code are excluded.
These data retain their source terms, separate from the platform code license.
NL4Opt's MIT notice and MAMO's CC-BY-SA-4.0 license are retained as
server/examples_data/NL4Opt-LICENSE.txt and server/examples_data/MAMO-LICENSE.txt.
The OPT-Agent snapshot does not specify individual licenses for its other
prepared datasets; the catalog records that absence without assigning one.

